  [1mMy recommendation: the first.[0m "Track who logged in" is an identity fact the server owns; threading it in as a
  parameter means the client is asserting who it is, which is exactly the thing you can't rely on. But if you have an
  upstream caller that genuinely already holds a [38;5;153muserId[39m (a test harness, an SSO layer), the second is the right read of
  your request and I'll do that.

